IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mv-act`

-- Motor Vehicles (Third-Party Risks and Compensation) Act 1960 -- worked cases.
--
-- Claims about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The boundary
-- cases are the point: the relevant amount, the 7-day notice, and the two-part
-- employment exclusion are where an answer changes.

§ `Fixtures`

-- s 2: the relevant amount is $5,000 unless the Minister prescribes another.
-- Both are used below, to show that no rule here depends on the figure.
`the statutory $5,000` MEANS Prescribed WITH `the relevant amount in dollars` IS 5000
`a prescribed $20,000` MEANS Prescribed WITH `the relevant amount in dollars` IS 20000

`an ordinary claimant` MEANS Claimant WITH
    `name` IS "Rajan"
    `below 21 years of age when the judgment was given` IS FALSE
    `lacks capacity within the Mental Capacity Act 2008 section 4 when the judgment was given` IS FALSE
    `unrepresented when the judgment was given` IS FALSE
    `isolated under the Infectious Diseases Act 1976 section 15 when the judgment was given` IS FALSE
    `in legal custody in a place of detention when the judgment was given` IS FALSE

`a claimant aged 19` MEANS Claimant WITH
    `name` IS "Siti"
    `below 21 years of age when the judgment was given` IS TRUE
    `lacks capacity within the Mental Capacity Act 2008 section 4 when the judgment was given` IS FALSE
    `unrepresented when the judgment was given` IS FALSE
    `isolated under the Infectious Diseases Act 1976 section 15 when the judgment was given` IS FALSE
    `in legal custody in a place of detention when the judgment was given` IS FALSE

`a compliant policy` MEANS Policy WITH
    `in force in relation to this use` IS TRUE
    `the insurer was lawfully carrying on motor insurance business in Singapore when issued` IS TRUE
    `insures the user against liability for death or bodily injury arising out of the use of the vehicle` IS TRUE
    `a certificate of insurance has been issued under section 4(9)` IS TRUE

`a policy from an unlicensed insurer` MEANS Policy WITH
    `in force in relation to this use` IS TRUE
    `the insurer was lawfully carrying on motor insurance business in Singapore when issued` IS FALSE
    `insures the user against liability for death or bodily injury arising out of the use of the vehicle` IS TRUE
    `a certificate of insurance has been issued under section 4(9)` IS TRUE

`no policy at all` MEANS Policy WITH
    `in force in relation to this use` IS FALSE
    `the insurer was lawfully carrying on motor insurance business in Singapore when issued` IS FALSE
    `insures the user against liability for death or bodily injury arising out of the use of the vehicle` IS FALSE
    `a certificate of insurance has been issued under section 4(9)` IS FALSE

`an ordinary road accident liability` MEANS Liability WITH
    `for death or bodily injury caused by or arising out of the use of the vehicle` IS TRUE
    `the injured person is in the employment of a person insured by the policy` IS FALSE
    `the injury arose out of and in the course of that employment` IS FALSE
    `the injured person is a platform worker providing a platform service for a platform operator insured by the policy` IS FALSE
    `the injury arose out of and in the course of providing that platform service` IS FALSE
    `it is a contractual liability` IS FALSE

§§ `4(4) -- the employment exclusion needs BOTH limbs`

-- An employee injured in the course of employment: outside the required cover.
`an employee injured at work` MEANS Liability WITH
    `for death or bodily injury caused by or arising out of the use of the vehicle` IS TRUE
    `the injured person is in the employment of a person insured by the policy` IS TRUE
    `the injury arose out of and in the course of that employment` IS TRUE
    `the injured person is a platform worker providing a platform service for a platform operator insured by the policy` IS FALSE
    `the injury arose out of and in the course of providing that platform service` IS FALSE
    `it is a contractual liability` IS FALSE

-- The SAME employee, off duty. Status alone does not take the liability out:
-- s 4(4)(a)(i) requires the injury to arise "out of and in the course of" the
-- employment as well. This pair is the whole content of the limb.
`an employee injured off duty` MEANS Liability WITH
    `for death or bodily injury caused by or arising out of the use of the vehicle` IS TRUE
    `the injured person is in the employment of a person insured by the policy` IS TRUE
    `the injury arose out of and in the course of that employment` IS FALSE
    `the injured person is a platform worker providing a platform service for a platform operator insured by the policy` IS FALSE
    `the injury arose out of and in the course of providing that platform service` IS FALSE
    `it is a contractual liability` IS FALSE

-- A platform worker on a delivery: the limb added by Act 30 of 2024.
`a platform worker on a delivery` MEANS Liability WITH
    `for death or bodily injury caused by or arising out of the use of the vehicle` IS TRUE
    `the injured person is in the employment of a person insured by the policy` IS FALSE
    `the injury arose out of and in the course of that employment` IS FALSE
    `the injured person is a platform worker providing a platform service for a platform operator insured by the policy` IS TRUE
    `the injury arose out of and in the course of providing that platform service` IS TRUE
    `it is a contractual liability` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the liability is required to be covered by section 4(1)(b)` `an ordinary road accident liability`
#ASSERT NOT `the liability is required to be covered by section 4(1)(b)` `an employee injured at work`
#ASSERT `the liability is required to be covered by section 4(1)(b)` `an employee injured off duty`
#ASSERT NOT `the liability is required to be covered by section 4(1)(b)` `a platform worker on a delivery`

§§ `3 -- the compulsory insurance offence and the employee's defence`

`driving uninsured in Singapore` MEANS Use WITH
    `the user` IS "Kumar"
    `the vehicle is used in Singapore` IS TRUE
    `the vehicle is registered in Singapore and used in a territory specified in the Schedule` IS FALSE
    `the policy` IS `no policy at all`
    `a complying security is in force in respect of third-party risks` IS FALSE

`driving insured in Singapore` MEANS Use WITH
    `the user` IS "Kumar"
    `the vehicle is used in Singapore` IS TRUE
    `the vehicle is registered in Singapore and used in a territory specified in the Schedule` IS FALSE
    `the policy` IS `a compliant policy`
    `a complying security is in force in respect of third-party risks` IS FALSE

-- A policy in force, but from an insurer not lawfully carrying on motor
-- insurance business: s 4(1)(a) fails, so the policy does not comply and the
-- use is still unlawful. The driver who believes they are insured is not.
`driving on a non-complying policy` MEANS Use WITH
    `the user` IS "Kumar"
    `the vehicle is used in Singapore` IS TRUE
    `the vehicle is registered in Singapore and used in a territory specified in the Schedule` IS FALSE
    `the policy` IS `a policy from an unlicensed insurer`
    `a complying security is in force in respect of third-party risks` IS FALSE

-- s 3(1) offers a security as an alternative to a policy.
`driving on a security instead of a policy` MEANS Use WITH
    `the user` IS "Kumar"
    `the vehicle is used in Singapore` IS TRUE
    `the vehicle is registered in Singapore and used in a territory specified in the Schedule` IS FALSE
    `the policy` IS `no policy at all`
    `a complying security is in force in respect of third-party risks` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the use contravenes section 3(1)` `driving uninsured in Singapore`
#ASSERT NOT `the use contravenes section 3(1)` `driving insured in Singapore`
#ASSERT `the use contravenes section 3(1)` `driving on a non-complying policy`
#ASSERT NOT `the use contravenes section 3(1)` `driving on a security instead of a policy`

`the full employee defence` MEANS Section3Defence WITH
    `the vehicle did not belong to the person and was not in the person's possession under a contract of hiring or loan` IS TRUE
    `the person was using the vehicle in the course of the person's employment` IS TRUE
    `the person neither knew nor had reason to believe that no complying cover was in force` IS TRUE

-- The employee who did suspect: limb (c) fails and the defence goes with it.
`an employee who suspected the truth` MEANS Section3Defence WITH
    `the vehicle did not belong to the person and was not in the person's possession under a contract of hiring or loan` IS TRUE
    `the person was using the vehicle in the course of the person's employment` IS TRUE
    `the person neither knew nor had reason to believe that no complying cover was in force` IS FALSE

`no defence at all` MEANS Section3Defence WITH
    `the vehicle did not belong to the person and was not in the person's possession under a contract of hiring or loan` IS FALSE
    `the person was using the vehicle in the course of the person's employment` IS FALSE
    `the person neither knew nor had reason to believe that no complying cover was in force` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 3` `driving uninsured in Singapore` `no defence at all`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 3` `driving uninsured in Singapore` `the full employee defence`
#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 3` `driving uninsured in Singapore` `an employee who suspected the truth`

-- s 3(3): disqualification follows conviction unless the court finds special
-- reasons. The pair shows the escape doing its work.
#ASSERT `the person is to be disqualified for 12 months under section 3(3)` `driving uninsured in Singapore` `no defence at all` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the person is to be disqualified for 12 months under section 3(3)` `driving uninsured in Singapore` `no defence at all` TRUE

§§ `9 -- the relevant amount, and the four bars`

`a judgment for $4,000` MEANS Judgment WITH
    `the claimant` IS `an ordinary claimant`
    `the policy` IS `a compliant policy`
    `the liability` IS `an ordinary road accident liability`
    `the liability is covered by the terms of the policy` IS TRUE
    `obtained against a person insured by the policy` IS TRUE
    `the sum payable excluding costs and interest in dollars` IS 4000
    `the judgment requires the sum to be paid to the Public Trustee` IS FALSE
    `the insurer had notice of the bringing of the proceedings before or within 7 days after they commenced` IS TRUE
    `enforcement on the judgment is stayed pending an appeal` IS FALSE
    `the policy was cancelled by mutual consent or under the policy before the event` IS FALSE
    `the certificate was surrendered or a statutory declaration of loss made before the event` IS FALSE
    `the certificate was surrendered or such a declaration made within 14 days after the cancellation took effect` IS FALSE
    `the insurer commenced proceedings for failure to surrender the certificate within the 14 day period` IS FALSE
    `the insurer obtained a declaration of entitlement to avoid for non-disclosure or misrepresentation in an action commenced before or within 3 months after the proceedings` IS FALSE

`a judgment for exactly $5,000` MEANS Judgment WITH
    `the claimant` IS `an ordinary claimant`
    `the policy` IS `a compliant policy`
    `the liability` IS `an ordinary road accident liability`
    `the liability is covered by the terms of the policy` IS TRUE
    `obtained against a person insured by the policy` IS TRUE
    `the sum payable excluding costs and interest in dollars` IS 5000
    `the judgment requires the sum to be paid to the Public Trustee` IS FALSE
    `the insurer had notice of the bringing of the proceedings before or within 7 days after they commenced` IS TRUE
    `enforcement on the judgment is stayed pending an appeal` IS FALSE
    `the policy was cancelled by mutual consent or under the policy before the event` IS FALSE
    `the certificate was surrendered or a statutory declaration of loss made before the event` IS FALSE
    `the certificate was surrendered or such a declaration made within 14 days after the cancellation took effect` IS FALSE
    `the insurer commenced proceedings for failure to surrender the certificate within the 14 day period` IS FALSE
    `the insurer obtained a declaration of entitlement to avoid for non-disclosure or misrepresentation in an action commenced before or within 3 months after the proceedings` IS FALSE

`a judgment for $5,001` MEANS Judgment WITH
    `the claimant` IS `an ordinary claimant`
    `the policy` IS `a compliant policy`
    `the liability` IS `an ordinary road accident liability`
    `the liability is covered by the terms of the policy` IS TRUE
    `obtained against a person insured by the policy` IS TRUE
    `the sum payable excluding costs and interest in dollars` IS 5001
    `the judgment requires the sum to be paid to the Public Trustee` IS FALSE
    `the insurer had notice of the bringing of the proceedings before or within 7 days after they commenced` IS TRUE
    `enforcement on the judgment is stayed pending an appeal` IS FALSE
    `the policy was cancelled by mutual consent or under the policy before the event` IS FALSE
    `the certificate was surrendered or a statutory declaration of loss made before the event` IS FALSE
    `the certificate was surrendered or such a declaration made within 14 days after the cancellation took effect` IS FALSE
    `the insurer commenced proceedings for failure to surrender the certificate within the 14 day period` IS FALSE
    `the insurer obtained a declaration of entitlement to avoid for non-disclosure or misrepresentation in an action commenced before or within 3 months after the proceedings` IS FALSE

-- THE BOUNDARY. "does not exceed" in (a) and "exceeds" in (b) put the relevant
-- amount itself on the permissive side: at exactly $5,000 the insurer MAY pay;
-- one dollar more and it MUST.
#ASSERT `the insurer may pay the claimant under section 9(1)(a)` `a judgment for $4,000` `the statutory $5,000`
#ASSERT `the insurer may pay the claimant under section 9(1)(a)` `a judgment for exactly $5,000` `the statutory $5,000`
#ASSERT NOT `the insurer must pay under section 9(1)(b)` `a judgment for exactly $5,000` `the statutory $5,000`
#ASSERT `the insurer must pay under section 9(1)(b)` `a judgment for $5,001` `the statutory $5,000`
#ASSERT NOT `the insurer may pay the claimant under section 9(1)(a)` `a judgment for $5,001` `the statutory $5,000`

-- The same judgment against a prescribed amount of $20,000: the figure is not
-- in the rules, so a Ministerial order moves the line and nothing else changes.
#ASSERT `the insurer may pay the claimant under section 9(1)(a)` `a judgment for $5,001` `a prescribed $20,000`
#ASSERT NOT `the insurer must pay under section 9(1)(b)` `a judgment for $5,001` `a prescribed $20,000`

§§ `9(1)(b)(i) -- routing to the Public Trustee`

-- A specified person, and the judgment requires payment to the Public Trustee:
-- both limbs are needed.
`a judgment for $9,000 to a 19 year old, payable to the Public Trustee` MEANS Judgment WITH
    `the claimant` IS `a claimant aged 19`
    `the policy` IS `a compliant policy`
    `the liability` IS `an ordinary road accident liability`
    `the liability is covered by the terms of the policy` IS TRUE
    `obtained against a person insured by the policy` IS TRUE
    `the sum payable excluding costs and interest in dollars` IS 9000
    `the judgment requires the sum to be paid to the Public Trustee` IS TRUE
    `the insurer had notice of the bringing of the proceedings before or within 7 days after they commenced` IS TRUE
    `enforcement on the judgment is stayed pending an appeal` IS FALSE
    `the policy was cancelled by mutual consent or under the policy before the event` IS FALSE
    `the certificate was surrendered or a statutory declaration of loss made before the event` IS FALSE
    `the certificate was surrendered or such a declaration made within 14 days after the cancellation took effect` IS FALSE
    `the insurer commenced proceedings for failure to surrender the certificate within the 14 day period` IS FALSE
    `the insurer obtained a declaration of entitlement to avoid for non-disclosure or misrepresentation in an action commenced before or within 3 months after the proceedings` IS FALSE

-- Same claimant and sum, but the judgment does not so require.
`a judgment for $9,000 to a 19 year old, silent on the Public Trustee` MEANS Judgment WITH
    `the claimant` IS `a claimant aged 19`
    `the policy` IS `a compliant policy`
    `the liability` IS `an ordinary road accident liability`
    `the liability is covered by the terms of the policy` IS TRUE
    `obtained against a person insured by the policy` IS TRUE
    `the sum payable excluding costs and interest in dollars` IS 9000
    `the judgment requires the sum to be paid to the Public Trustee` IS FALSE
    `the insurer had notice of the bringing of the proceedings before or within 7 days after they commenced` IS TRUE
    `enforcement on the judgment is stayed pending an appeal` IS FALSE
    `the policy was cancelled by mutual consent or under the policy before the event` IS FALSE
    `the certificate was surrendered or a statutory declaration of loss made before the event` IS FALSE
    `the certificate was surrendered or such a declaration made within 14 days after the cancellation took effect` IS FALSE
    `the insurer commenced proceedings for failure to surrender the certificate within the 14 day period` IS FALSE
    `the insurer obtained a declaration of entitlement to avoid for non-disclosure or misrepresentation in an action commenced before or within 3 months after the proceedings` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the claimant is a specified person for section 9` `a claimant aged 19`
#ASSERT NOT `the claimant is a specified person for section 9` `an ordinary claimant`
#ASSERT `payment must be made to the Public Trustee` `a judgment for $9,000 to a 19 year old, payable to the Public Trustee` `the statutory $5,000`
#ASSERT NOT `payment must be made to the Public Trustee` `a judgment for $9,000 to a 19 year old, silent on the Public Trustee` `the statutory $5,000`
#ASSERT `payment must be made to the claimant under section 9(1)(b)(ii)` `a judgment for $9,000 to a 19 year old, silent on the Public Trustee` `the statutory $5,000`

§§ `9(6) and 9(7) -- the four bars`

-- s 9(6)(a): no notice within 7 days of the proceedings commencing.
`a judgment where the insurer was never notified` MEANS Judgment WITH
    `the claimant` IS `an ordinary claimant`
    `the policy` IS `a compliant policy`
    `the liability` IS `an ordinary road accident liability`
    `the liability is covered by the terms of the policy` IS TRUE
    `obtained against a person insured by the policy` IS TRUE
    `the sum payable excluding costs and interest in dollars` IS 9000
    `the judgment requires the sum to be paid to the Public Trustee` IS FALSE
    `the insurer had notice of the bringing of the proceedings before or within 7 days after they commenced` IS FALSE
    `enforcement on the judgment is stayed pending an appeal` IS FALSE
    `the policy was cancelled by mutual consent or under the policy before the event` IS FALSE
    `the certificate was surrendered or a statutory declaration of loss made before the event` IS FALSE
    `the certificate was surrendered or such a declaration made within 14 days after the cancellation took effect` IS FALSE
    `the insurer commenced proceedings for failure to surrender the certificate within the 14 day period` IS FALSE
    `the insurer obtained a declaration of entitlement to avoid for non-disclosure or misrepresentation in an action commenced before or within 3 months after the proceedings` IS FALSE

-- s 9(6)(c): cancelled before the event AND the certificate surrendered.
-- Cancellation alone is not enough -- the Act requires one of the three
-- certificate dealings as well.
`a judgment where the policy was cancelled and the certificate surrendered` MEANS Judgment WITH
    `the claimant` IS `an ordinary claimant`
    `the policy` IS `a compliant policy`
    `the liability` IS `an ordinary road accident liability`
    `the liability is covered by the terms of the policy` IS TRUE
    `obtained against a person insured by the policy` IS TRUE
    `the sum payable excluding costs and interest in dollars` IS 9000
    `the judgment requires the sum to be paid to the Public Trustee` IS FALSE
    `the insurer had notice of the bringing of the proceedings before or within 7 days after they commenced` IS TRUE
    `enforcement on the judgment is stayed pending an appeal` IS FALSE
    `the policy was cancelled by mutual consent or under the policy before the event` IS TRUE
    `the certificate was surrendered or a statutory declaration of loss made before the event` IS TRUE
    `the certificate was surrendered or such a declaration made within 14 days after the cancellation took effect` IS FALSE
    `the insurer commenced proceedings for failure to surrender the certificate within the 14 day period` IS FALSE
    `the insurer obtained a declaration of entitlement to avoid for non-disclosure or misrepresentation in an action commenced before or within 3 months after the proceedings` IS FALSE

`a judgment where the policy was cancelled but the certificate kept` MEANS Judgment WITH
    `the claimant` IS `an ordinary claimant`
    `the policy` IS `a compliant policy`
    `the liability` IS `an ordinary road accident liability`
    `the liability is covered by the terms of the policy` IS TRUE
    `obtained against a person insured by the policy` IS TRUE
    `the sum payable excluding costs and interest in dollars` IS 9000
    `the judgment requires the sum to be paid to the Public Trustee` IS FALSE
    `the insurer had notice of the bringing of the proceedings before or within 7 days after they commenced` IS TRUE
    `enforcement on the judgment is stayed pending an appeal` IS FALSE
    `the policy was cancelled by mutual consent or under the policy before the event` IS TRUE
    `the certificate was surrendered or a statutory declaration of loss made before the event` IS FALSE
    `the certificate was surrendered or such a declaration made within 14 days after the cancellation took effect` IS FALSE
    `the insurer commenced proceedings for failure to surrender the certificate within the 14 day period` IS FALSE
    `the insurer obtained a declaration of entitlement to avoid for non-disclosure or misrepresentation in an action commenced before or within 3 months after the proceedings` IS FALSE

-- s 9(7): a declaration of entitlement to avoid, obtained in time.
`a judgment defeated by a section 9(7) declaration` MEANS Judgment WITH
    `the claimant` IS `an ordinary claimant`
    `the policy` IS `a compliant policy`
    `the liability` IS `an ordinary road accident liability`
    `the liability is covered by the terms of the policy` IS TRUE
    `obtained against a person insured by the policy` IS TRUE
    `the sum payable excluding costs and interest in dollars` IS 9000
    `the judgment requires the sum to be paid to the Public Trustee` IS FALSE
    `the insurer had notice of the bringing of the proceedings before or within 7 days after they commenced` IS TRUE
    `enforcement on the judgment is stayed pending an appeal` IS FALSE
    `the policy was cancelled by mutual consent or under the policy before the event` IS FALSE
    `the certificate was surrendered or a statutory declaration of loss made before the event` IS FALSE
    `the certificate was surrendered or such a declaration made within 14 days after the cancellation took effect` IS FALSE
    `the insurer commenced proceedings for failure to surrender the certificate within the 14 day period` IS FALSE
    `the insurer obtained a declaration of entitlement to avoid for non-disclosure or misrepresentation in an action commenced before or within 3 months after the proceedings` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `no sum is payable by the insurer` `a judgment where the insurer was never notified`
#ASSERT NOT `the insurer must pay under section 9(1)(b)` `a judgment where the insurer was never notified` `the statutory $5,000`

#ASSERT `no sum is payable by the insurer` `a judgment where the policy was cancelled and the certificate surrendered`
-- Cancelled, but no certificate dealing: s 9(6)(c) does NOT bar, and the
-- insurer must still pay. This is the pair that shows (c) has two halves.
#ASSERT NOT `no sum is payable by the insurer` `a judgment where the policy was cancelled but the certificate kept`
#ASSERT `the insurer must pay under section 9(1)(b)` `a judgment where the policy was cancelled but the certificate kept` `the statutory $5,000`

#ASSERT `no sum is payable by the insurer` `a judgment defeated by a section 9(7) declaration`

§§ `9(1) -- the gateway`

-- An employee injured in the course of employment: the liability is not one
-- s 4(1)(b) requires to be covered, so s 9(1) never engages however large the
-- judgment and however punctual the notice.
`a judgment on an excluded employment liability` MEANS Judgment WITH
    `the claimant` IS `an ordinary claimant`
    `the policy` IS `a compliant policy`
    `the liability` IS `an employee injured at work`
    `the liability is covered by the terms of the policy` IS TRUE
    `obtained against a person insured by the policy` IS TRUE
    `the sum payable excluding costs and interest in dollars` IS 50000
    `the judgment requires the sum to be paid to the Public Trustee` IS FALSE
    `the insurer had notice of the bringing of the proceedings before or within 7 days after they commenced` IS TRUE
    `enforcement on the judgment is stayed pending an appeal` IS FALSE
    `the policy was cancelled by mutual consent or under the policy before the event` IS FALSE
    `the certificate was surrendered or a statutory declaration of loss made before the event` IS FALSE
    `the certificate was surrendered or such a declaration made within 14 days after the cancellation took effect` IS FALSE
    `the insurer commenced proceedings for failure to surrender the certificate within the 14 day period` IS FALSE
    `the insurer obtained a declaration of entitlement to avoid for non-disclosure or misrepresentation in an action commenced before or within 3 months after the proceedings` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `section 9(1) is engaged` `a judgment on an excluded employment liability`
#ASSERT NOT `the insurer must pay under section 9(1)(b)` `a judgment on an excluded employment liability` `the statutory $5,000`
#ASSERT `section 9(1) is engaged` `a judgment for $5,001`
